From 02393e6ca3919b4ca765afef9ab4d97ad11e75a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:09:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xen: domctl: zero the createdomain hypercall argument

xen_domctl_createdomain() is the only function in drivers/xen/dom0/domctl.c
that declares its xen_domctl_t without an initialiser; the others use a
designated initialiser, which zeroes the members they do not name. It is also
the one where that matters.

struct xen_domctl_createdomain ends in struct xen_arch_domainconfig, and the
copy `domctl.u.createdomain = *config` only sets what this tree's definition of
that struct names. The definition comes from zephyr-xenlib's copy of the Xen
4.21 public headers, while the hypervisor is Xen 4.22. Both are 16 bytes on
arm64, but 4.22 puts its new v8r_el1_msa field where 4.21 has padding. Today's
caller (xenlib's domain creation) memsets its config, and a whole-struct copy
usually carries those zero bytes along - but the value of padding after a
struct assignment is unspecified, so nothing guarantees what Xen reads there.
Zeroing the argument makes it XEN_DOMCTL_CONFIG_ARM_V8R_EL1_MSA_NONE, which
v8r_el1_msa_domain_sanitise_config() accepts on a non-MPU build; the same holds
for any field a later Xen adds in padding this tree does not name.

Upstream fixed the comma typo in the same three assignments (fc146cab757);
the initialiser is still missing in v4.5.0.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/xen/dom0/domctl.c b/drivers/xen/dom0/domctl.c
index d524e5dc4b..8ae171e3ce 100644
--- a/drivers/xen/dom0/domctl.c
+++ b/drivers/xen/dom0/domctl.c
@@ -318,7 +318,17 @@ int xen_domctl_max_vcpus(int domid, int max_vcpus)
 int xen_domctl_createdomain(int *domid, struct xen_domctl_createdomain *config)
 {
 	int ret;
-	xen_domctl_t domctl;
+	/*
+	 * Zero the whole hypercall argument. This is the only xen_domctl_t in
+	 * this file without an initialiser, and it is the one that matters:
+	 * struct xen_domctl_createdomain ends in xen_arch_domainconfig, and a
+	 * newer Xen can define a field where this tree's headers only have
+	 * padding (Xen 4.22's v8r_el1_msa, against zephyr-xenlib's 4.21
+	 * headers). The copy below sets only the members this tree names, and
+	 * the value of padding after a struct assignment is unspecified, so the
+	 * hypervisor could otherwise read whatever was on the stack there.
+	 */
+	xen_domctl_t domctl = { 0 };
 
 	if (!domid || !config) {
 		return -EINVAL;
